    "title": "I came across this today. If you don\u2019t have time to read it, Canva has cut 22% of its workforce (around 1,270 jobs) \ud83d\ude33\n\nThis was founder Melanie Perkins\u2019 letter to those affected: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/news/canva-team-update/\n\nIt\u2019s an interesting read. Alongside what appears to be a pretty impressive exit package (6 months salary, keeping the work Macbook and career transition support including access to startup/community project grants), the comms seems to come from a place of genuine compassion. \n\nWhile making redundancies isn\u2019t pleasant for anyone involved, I strongly believe that by applying some humanity, it can be done \u2018well\u2019. (Even without the sweeteners.)\n\nWhat\u2019s your experience of redundancy handled well - what made the difference? | Mustard HR",
